    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0632" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/2332</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Alexandria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the request of Red Cross ask British authorities if they can provide quick
                    transportation to Saloniki for cargo discharged from <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caesar</hi>. If transportation can be provided make immediate arrangements
                    to forward all serviceable cargo for relief situation Saloniki.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d672-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d672-f1" n="1" xml:id="d672-f1-content">
                <p>In a telegram of Sept. 25 the Consul reported: “Entire consignment now loading.”
                    (File No. 811.142/2391.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
